  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'biophilia' was first introduced by biologist E.O. Wilson in his book 'Biophilia'. He argued that humans have an innate love for nature and that this connection is essential to our well-being. However, as we increasingly urbanize and spend more time indoors, this bond with the natural world is being eroded. In fact, studies have shown that people who live in cities tend to have lower levels of vitamin D, which is crucial for bone health, due to reduced exposure to sunlight.\n\nWilson also suggested that biophilia can be cultivated through activities such as gardening, bird-watching, and simply spending time outdoors. He believed that by reconnecting with nature, we can not only improve our physical health but also enhance our mental well-being and creativity. While some critics have argued that Wilson's ideas are too simplistic or romanticized, his work has had a significant impact on the field of environmental psychology.\n\nIn recent years, there has been a growing interest in applying biophilia to urban planning and design. Architects and city planners are now incorporating elements such as green roofs, parks, and public gardens into their designs to promote a sense of connection to nature. This approach not only improves air quality but also provides residents with opportunities for physical activity and social interaction.\n\nWhile the concept of biophilia is still evolving, its potential to transform our relationship with the natural world cannot be overstated. By recognizing the importance of this innate love for nature, we can work towards creating a more sustainable and harmonious coexistence between humans and the environment.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of E.O. Wilson's book 'Biophilia'?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It describes the negative impact of urbanization on human health.\", \"It argues that humans have an innate love for nature and its importance for our well-being.\", \"It provides practical tips for reducing air pollution in cities.\", \"It explores the relationship between vitamin D levels and bone health.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It argues that humans have an innate love for nature and its importance for our well-being.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is a potential consequence of reduced exposure to sunlight?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Increased risk of skin cancer.\", \"Lower levels of vitamin D, which can affect bone health.\", \"Improved air quality in urban areas.\", \"Reduced greenhouse gas emissions.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Lower levels of vitamin D, which can affect bone health.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"According to Wilson, what is a way to cultivate biophilia?\",\n      \"options\": [\"By spending more time indoors and using air conditioning.\", \"Through activities such as gardening or bird-watching.\", \"By focusing on reducing carbon emissions in cities.\", \"By ignoring the natural world and its importance for human well-being.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Through activities such as gardening or bird-watching.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is an example of how biophilia is being applied to urban planning?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The construction of skyscrapers and high-rise buildings.\", \"The incorporation of green roofs, parks, and public gardens into city designs.\", \"The implementation of strict recycling policies in cities.\", \"The promotion of electric vehicles as a primary mode of transportation.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The incorporation of green roofs, parks, and public gardens into city designs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards Wilson's ideas?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and dismissive.\", \"Neutral and objective.\", \"Positive and supportive.\", \"Ambivalent and uncertain.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Positive and supportive.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
